#---
# purpose: "a guard on a receive clause selects the message on every door"
# oracle: oracle.exs
#---
#
# # receive_guard_clauses
#
# Guards reach dispatch as a `Region::Guard`, and the three doors decide that
# region independently. Every behavioural fixture exercising a guard did so on
# entry dispatch — a `when` on a function head — so the receive matcher's guard
# path had no coverage at all, on any door.
#
# That is the blind spot this arc keeps finding. Coverage of a region is not
# coverage of a region AT A DISPATCH SITE: `map_key` and `map_kind` were
# exercised only inside `receive`, and interpreted entry dispatch turned out to
# never match a binary-keyed map pattern because it passed an empty prepared-key
# map. The same asymmetry, pointing the other way, is this fixture.
#
# ## What it covers
#
#   * clause order among guards on the same message shape — the first guard
#     that holds wins, so `5` must reach the `< 10` clause and not `< 100`;
#   * a guard that rejects every clause but the last, unguarded one;
#   * a guard combined with a pattern, so both the pattern region and the guard
#     region have to agree before the clause is chosen;
#   * selective receive: a message that matches no clause stays in the mailbox
#     and is delivered to a later `receive`, rather than being consumed.
def main() do
  send(self(), 5)
  send(self(), 50)
  send(self(), 500)
  dbg(classify())
  dbg(classify())
  dbg(classify())

  send(self(), {:count, 0})
  send(self(), {:count, 7})
  dbg(counted())
  dbg(counted())

  # `:skip` matches no clause of `only_tuples/0`, so it is left in the mailbox
  # and the tuple behind it is taken first.
  send(self(), :skip)
  send(self(), {:take, 1})
  dbg(only_tuples())
  dbg(anything())
end

defp classify() do
  receive do
    n when n < 10 -> {:small, n}
    n when n < 100 -> {:medium, n}
    n -> {:large, n}
  end
end

defp counted() do
  receive do
    {:count, n} when n > 0 -> {:positive, n}
    {:count, n} -> {:zero_or_less, n}
  end
end

defp only_tuples() do
  receive do
    {:take, n} -> {:took, n}
  end
end

defp anything() do
  receive do
    other -> {:leftover, other}
  end
end
